<newsitem itemid="59631" id="root" date="1996-09-17" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Alliance &amp; Leicester H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Alliance &amp; Leicester H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Pretax profit		183		  vs 163</p>
<p> Operating profit *	 192		  vs 163</p>
<p> Bad/doubtful debt charge 5.4		  vs nil</p>
<p> Tax paid		     63.7		 vs 53.8</p>
<p>* NOTE - before conversion costs of 8.6 million stg  </p>
<p> Net taxed		    119.7		vs 109.4</p>
<p> Net interest income	469.6		vs 552.7</p>
<p> Administrative expenses  349.6		vs 342.5</p>
<p>NOTE - UK building society Alliance &amp; Leicester, which is planning to convert to bank status via a stock market flotation next year, said it had established a strong financial basis for conversion and plans for the change were well on course.</p>
<p>Total assets increased to 23,369 million stg, compared to 22,846 million stg at the end of December 1995 and 23,014 million stg at the end of June 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
